<h2 id="aaahc">AAAHC Alignment, Explained</h2>
<p>Our policies and protocols are built to align with the standards of the Accreditation Association for Ambulatory Health Care (AAAHC). Alignment means your clinic is positioned to pursue AAAHC accreditation if and when it chooses to — the groundwork is already in place.</p>
<p>To be clear about what that does and doesn't mean: Regenitiva is not itself AAAHC-accredited, and building an aligned program is not the same as being accredited. Accreditation is a separate step each clinic pursues on its own. What we provide is a framework designed so that step is straightforward rather than a rebuild.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <div class="callout-label">Why this matters</div>
  <p class="callout-body">Programs built without documented policies, training records, and a real audit schedule are the ones that don't hold up under a payer audit. We build the record as the program is built, so the documentation matches the practice instead of being reconstructed after a question comes up.</p>
</div>

